Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): model-callable kanban_archive tool over the CLI
 archive path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Archive is CLI-only today: a profile restricted to the kanban toolset can
create, comment, block and complete cards in-session but cannot archive a
finished card without a terminal. This adds kanban_archive(task_id, board?)
as a thin wrapper over the exact kanban_db.archive_task() the CLI
`hermes kanban archive` routes through — zero new DB logic, zero behavior
divergence (#76196 worker termination, reclaimed-run close, child-promote
and workspace reap all ride the proven path; the tool is deliberately not
stricter than the CLI on running+claimed cards).

Access model (the open question from the anchor issue): lifecycle gate —
visible to any profile holding the kanban toolset and to dispatcher
workers, same registration pattern as kanban_block/kanban_complete.
kanban_list/kanban_unblock stay orchestrator-only. Board pinning reuses
the shared _board() helper (env/symlink resolution chain, explicit-slug
override). Unknown and already-archived ids report the sibling
not-found/CAS error shape via _existing_task/_check.

Refs: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/143206
